Hello @captainsafia 

The generator is indeed producing an output when the declaration is in a namespace, I proved this by quickly adding the below test to [PublicTopLevelProgramGeneratorTests.cs](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/main/src/Framework/AspNetCoreAnalyzers/test/SourceGenerators/PublicTopLevelProgramGeneratorTests.cs), which fails under the current logic.
```
[Fact]
public async Task DoesNotGeneratesSource_IfProgramIsAlreadyPublicInNamespace()
{
    var source = """
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Builder;

var app = WebApplication.Create();

app.MapGet("/", () => "Hello, World!");

app.Run();

namespace Foo
{
    public partial class Program { }
}
""";

    await VerifyCS.VerifyAsync(source);
}
```

Regarding the CS1591 compiler warning are we happy to do something like the below on generating the output?
```
// <auto-generated />
#pragma warning disable CS1591
public partial class Program { }
#pragma warning restore CS1591
```
